            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A child stroller frame (100) includes a first frame portion (1), a second frame portion (2), a pivoting part (3), and a linkage (5) movably coupling the first frame portion (1) to the pivoting part (3). The second frame portion (2) has a first end and a second end, the first end of the second frame portion (2) being pivotally connected with the first frame portion (1). The pivoting part (3) has one end fixedly connected with a rear wheel support member (4), and another end pivotally connected with the second frame portion (2). The linkage (5) includes a plurality of bars (511, 512, 521), a first one (511) of the bars being formed integrally as a single body having a first bar portion (5111) and a second bar portion (5112) that intersect each other at an angle, the second frame portion (2) being pivotally connected with the first bar (511) in a region thereof where the first bar portion (5111) joins with the second bar portion (5112), whereby the first frame portion (1) and the wheel support member (4) are movably linked for folding in a concurrent manner toward the second frame portion (2).</p>
            </abstract>
